{"what":"Road links of the masterplan inside the red line, survey m (x, y). Made offline for the plan drawing named in plan_svg_bytes; PlanBase draws them with his own roads and paths.","made":"2026-11-13","plan_svg_bytes":13038680,"method":["Which street runs where: the town's street bands (OpenStreetMap centrelines) inside the red line, used only to find the way; the parts that lie on a surveyed building (closed building outlines of the DWG, 537 m2) are left out, so no link runs through one. Each link is one ribbon with flat ends. Where the survey (DWG layers YOL_SOSE, YOL_TOPRAK, YOL_BORDUR, YOL_KOPRU) has road lines on both sides within 8 m, the ribbon's centre is moved across its own direction to the middle between those lines (59 % of the link length); elsewhere it keeps the street band's line. Half width = distance to the nearest survey line (road edge, kerb, bridge, building or wall line), so 3 to 9 m wide between road lines and 3 to 6 m elsewhere. Centre smoothed over about 8 m, width over about 30 m. Nothing is drawn where no existing street runs.","gate links (63 found, 17 left out): every town street that reaches the red line is continued on its existing line to the first road or path of the plan, when that is at most 150 m away and no new bridge is needed, and carried straight on past the red line. Left out: a street that runs within 5 m of his own paths for more than 60 % of its length, and a street under 40 m whose crossing of the red line is within 15 m of where his own path meets the red line (his path already is that street). Before that, 11 stubs under 15 m with a survey road line within 8 m on less than 30 % of their length were skipped. A street does not count as leaving where a house stands within 6 m straight ahead outside the red line (5 crossings; houses = the survey's building lines, the OpenStreetMap footprints the drawing uses and Data/houses_sat2023.json). Also left out: links more than 1.5 times longer than the straight line between their ends (1, hairpins round a block) and lanes that run along the red line (within 6 m for more than 60 % of their length) without survey road lines on both sides (14).","end links (24): every road, path or bridge end of the plan within 25 m of an existing street is led onto it and along it to the next plan road or path, or to the town street at the red line (at most 150 m, no new bridge). Not a loose end: an end within 5 m of the red line, or a short side spur or outward-pointing end of a path that meets the red line, with a town street or survey road line there; an end in the water. Where a link would run within 5 m of his own paths that part is not drawn (10 links shortened). Each link end is carried straight on to the centre line of his path. Left out: links that are no shortcut, where his own paths reach the same point at least as fast (12); parts of his plan under 50 m2 have no loose end and are no destination.","pieces (21): a piece is kept only if it joins two things (two parts of his plan, or his plan and the red line), is at least 20 m2 and lies at most 60 % on his own surfaces.","footbridges (4): where his dotted route crosses the water with no bridge surface drawn, a 3.0 m deck under the route. ASSUMPTION: the 3.0 m width; his drawing gives the bridge only as a line.","joins (17): a road or path end of the plan with no existing street to follow is carried on in its own drawn direction (straight, or turned at most 35 degrees as a curve) until it meets the next road or path, at most 120 m, never through a building of his plan or a surveyed building, nor over water; same kind and width as the path it continues (curved ones at most 4 m wide). Of two joins side by side from one wide end, the shorter is kept.","routes: his dotted route lines moved to the centre line of the path they run on, where that centre is at most 5 m away, then smoothed over 7 m; elsewhere unchanged."],"limits":"Positions as good as the survey road lines where a link runs between them, else as good as the street bands (OpenStreetMap), kept clear of the survey's building and wall lines. Not checked against the 2023 satellite image link by link. 3 ends of the plan are left as he drew them (water or a building ahead, or no road within 120 m, or a pier into the lake): open_ends (frame m: along the frame from its west end, up).","links":[[[[30413.57,31389.06],[30422.23,31386.62],[30420.72,31381.25],[30419.75,31378.66],[30418.99,31378.01],[30425.98,31369.89],[30432.1,31375.04],[30433.39,31373.51],[30427.27,31368.36],[30437.17,31356.65],[30442.77,31350.73],[30445.46,31346.95],[30446.38,31344.7],[30446.65,31342.77],[30446.54,31341.0],[30446.26,31340.15],[30444.83,31331.95],[30437.39,31341.85],[30437.62,31342.56],[30436.89,31343.61],[30435.92,31344.89],[30431.97,31349.05],[30408.95,31379.65],[30410.01,31382.19],[30411.68,31383.64],[30411.99,31383.45]]],[[[30371.17,31506.84],[30375.48,31501.53],[30377.17,31498.69],[30377.55,31496.63],[30377.82,31490.54],[30369.16,31490.16],[30368.9,31496.05],[30369.02,31496.72],[30367.97,31499.21],[30366.38,31502.1],[30365.93,31502.47],[30364.93,31502.62],[30361.07,31502.59],[30358.82,31502.74],[30357.02,31503.18],[30354.06,31504.56],[30350.86,31513.49],[30359.79,31509.91],[30365.95,31509.4],[30368.75,31508.59]]],[[[30305.79,31654.09],[30310.58,31637.17],[30311.91,31633.45],[30313.48,31629.66],[30318.51,31618.55],[30329.51,31596.44],[30333.16,31588.66],[30334.61,31584.27],[30334.92,31582.34],[30335.45,31574.44],[30329.15,31574.02],[30300.32,31654.39],[30304.86,31656.37]]],[[[29841.36,32242.67],[29851.77,32238.7],[29857.06,32236.37],[29857.34,32237.5],[29866.54,32235.2],[29877.26,32232.19],[29880.65,32231.42],[29882.23,32231.53],[29882.72,32226.76],[29842.12,32235.86],[29838.73,32237.28],[29836.52,32238.48],[29834.36,32240.12],[29832.71,32242.49],[29832.19,32245.32],[29832.75,32247.88],[29835.62,32253.62],[29838.42,32259.84],[29840.02,32263.81],[29842.42,32267.3],[29846.11,32264.74],[29843.95,32261.65],[29842.89,32258.12],[298